{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_stj3bbo2sy5pphn7xii33mxt6de67euxtmnv3z535ef7bajkv7hq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe library is libsodium-style `hex2bin` — one C file, one exported function. The **Rust translation was already correct**; I found no divergences requiring fixes to `src/lib.rs`.\n\n**Phase A** — three artifacts in `translation/`:\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — C `.so` exports exactly one symbol (`hex2bin`); Rust exports it under the identical name. No module was skipped, no stubs exist. `strchr` is the only non-libc-satisfiable import, reimplemented as the private `strchr_found`.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 22 rows: 3 distinct `ret = -1` sites in the C, expanded into 11 error rows (including site-combination rows) + 11 generic FFI-boundary rows, plus a table of 3 conditions that are untestable without UB or >2 GiB inputs.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 9 branch axes derived from the C's `if`/loop conditions, pruned to 28 meaningful combinations.\n\n**Phases B & C** — `tests/harness/mod.rs` loads **both** `.so` files via `libloading` and compares return value, the entire `bin` buffer *plus an 8-byte guard region past `bin_maxlen`*, and the exact `*hex_end_p` offset. 28 Phase B tests + 22 Phase C tests, all passing, with fixed-seed randomized inputs (including a 20 000-case unstructured fuzz row and a full `0x00..=0xFF` byte sweep). Because `cargo test` doesn't emit a cdylib, the harness builds a fresh one into a separate `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` on every run, so a stale `.so` can never be tested.\n\n**Phase D** — `check_features.sh` enumerates features from `Cargo.toml` (there are none, so default and `--no-default-features` are the only configs), and per config runs `cargo check`, builds the `.so`, diffs `nm -D` both directions, and runs the full suite. Result: symbol diff empty, zero undefined non-libc symbols, all tests pass.\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n\n1. **The two initial test failures were bugs in my own expectation table, not in the Rust.** `assert_same` passed both times; the separate C-ground-truth pin caught that I had mis-derived the expected value. E.g. I claimed `\"ab:cd\"` with `ignore=\":\"` errors, but the `:` sits at index 2 — an *even* nibble boundary — so it is ignored and the call succeeds. I corrected `ERRORS.md`/the tests to match the C, and kept both variants as tests.\n\n2. **I added a mutation check (`mutation_check.sh`) because passing tests alone don't prove the harness can see anything.** It injects 8 deliberate bugs into `src/lib.rs` (off-by-one on the overflow check, dropping the `state == 0` guard on `ignore`, removing the `strchr` NUL-terminator match, removing the `hex_pos--` rewind, etc.). All 8 were killed and the original was restored and re-verified — confirming the differential suite is genuinely sensitive rather than vacuously green.\n\nI also added two config rows the axes implied but I'd initially missed: **in-place decoding** (`bin == hex`, legitimate usage where the C interleaves writes with reads at `bin_pos < hex_pos`) and `ignore` sets built from the input's own bytes. Both pass.\n\n`c_src/` is unmodified (md5sums of all three source files verified; only the instructed `build/` directory was added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4758,"cache_read_input_tokens":97329,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4758,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2787289-ec3f-4f95-b9da-0fa7f1ebd637","uuid":"2c7a4170-be55-4334-9190-01347a33e232","timestamp":"2026-08-26T22:16:55.876Z"}
